Given $a=2-i$ and $b=-1+i$, we need to find $2a+3b$.

First, we calculate $2a$:
\begin{align*}
2a &= 2(2-i) \\
&= 4 - 2i.
\end{align*}

Next, we calculate $3b$:
\begin{align*}
3b &= 3(-1+i) \\
&= -3 + 3i.
\end{align*}

Now, we add $2a$ and $3b$:
\begin{align*}
2a + 3b &= (4 - 2i) + (-3 + 3i) \\
&= 4 - 3 - 2i + 3i \\
&= 1 + i.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the final answer is $\boxed{1+i}$.
